Subject: [PATCH 10780/11171] Correct two of my own claims after the follow-up
 agent's independent check

Both corrections are to entries I filed today, verified in source before amending.

First, on the levels/receipt disagreement, I concluded "the receipt agrees with the
per-level record; the headline is the outlier". That is backwards.
arc_trajectory_supervisor.observe credits on `if int(snapshot.level) >
self._last_level` and never un-credits a later drop, so a 0 to 1 to 0 excursion that
banks nothing still sets resolved_by_levelup true on every pending redirect. cd82's
level_up_charged [771] and per_level[0].completed true record a real momentary
transition; levels 0 records that nothing was banked. Both are honest about
different things, and the final-frame delta is defensible as a banked-levels
measure. deepest_level_reached 0 is untouched by this and still hard to defend.

The practical rule is now stronger than the earlier caution: never read helped or
resolved_by_levelup as evidence of banked progress, because the credit does not even
require a level-up that lasts. Use banked levels or actions-to-progress.

Second, I briefed the follow-up agent that 28 unredirected stagnation windows were
the written specification for a new arm under REQ-ARC-WMTE-6640 rule 4. Wrong. Per
arc_supervisor_refinement._new_arm_cells, unredirected windows specify a new arm only
when all four curated arms have fired. Three fired; tool_loop_reinduction fired zero
because its flag was off. The 14 windows per game are arm exhaustion within a level,
not an unmet need. Enable the disabled arm, re-run, and only then does the ledger
become a new-arm spec -- which also keeps the AVO boundary intact, selection over a
curated set rather than model-generated proposal.

Recorded because a wrong premise in a task brief propagates into whatever that task
builds, and this one would have manufactured an arm nobody needed.

