+
+**CORRECTION 2026-09-02 16:00Z — my conclusion above was wrong, and the receipt is the looser of
+the two.** I wrote "the receipt agrees with the per-level record; the headline is the outlier."
+Verified in source, that is backwards.
+
+`arc_trajectory_supervisor.observe` credits on `if int(snapshot.level) > self._last_level`, then
+advances `_last_level`. It credits ANY increase in the LIVE level reading and never un-credits a
+later drop. So a 0 -> 1 -> 0 excursion that banks nothing still sets `resolved_by_levelup: true`
+on every pending redirect and records an `actions_to_levelup`.
+
+That explains cd82 exactly: `level_up_charged: [771]` and `per_level[0].completed: true` record a
+real momentary transition, and `levels: 0` records that nothing was BANKED. Both are honest about
+different things. The final-frame delta is defensible as a banked-levels measure, and my claim that
+it was "the outlier" does not survive.
+
+`deepest_level_reached: 0` remains hard to defend under either reading and is untouched by this
+correction.
+
+**Practical rule, from the follow-up agent's independent check:** never read `helped` /
+`resolved_by_levelup` as evidence of banked progress. Use banked levels or actions-to-progress.
+This is stronger than the earlier "one level-up credits every pending redirect" caution — the
+credit does not even require a level-up that lasts.
+
+**Related methodological correction, recorded so it is not repeated.** I briefed the follow-up
+agent that 28 `stagnations_unredirected` windows across two games were "the written specification
+for a NEW arm" per REQ-ARC-WMTE-6640 rule 4. That was wrong. Per
+`arc_supervisor_refinement._new_arm_cells`, unredirected windows specify a new arm only when
+`set(ARM_ORDER) <= arms_fired` — ALL FOUR curated arms must have fired first. Only three fired;
+`tool_loop_reinduction` fired zero times because `CARNOT_ARC_SUPERVISOR_TOOL_ARM` was OFF. The 14
+windows per game are ARM EXHAUSTION within a level, not an unmet need. The correct next step is to
+enable the disabled curated arm and re-run; only if all four fire and stagnation persists does the
+ledger become a new-arm specification. This also keeps the AVO boundary intact — selection over a
+curated set, never model-generated arm proposal.
+
